<title>UK: INSTANT VIEW - Political reaction to U.K. budget.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW - Political reaction to U.K. budget.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a selection of political reactions to Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke's 1996 annual budget statement.</p>
<p>For a full breakdown of budget news -  UK/BUDGET</p>
<p>GEOFFREY HOWE, FORMER U.K. FOREIGN MINISTER AND CHANCELLOR OF THE EXCHEQUER</p>
<p>&quot;I am pleased by the emphasis he's placed on vigialance against inflation and on really tough control of public spending. He has set himself on the right course by emphasising so much that this budget tightens fiscal policy.&quot;</p>
</text>
